.TH DARPA_SPILLSERVER 3 "September 2026" "darpa_spillserver 1.0.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
darpa_spillserver \- Python library for NOvA accelerator event timestamps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
.B from darpa_spillserver.config import load_config
.B from darpa_spillserver.app import create_app
.B from darpa_spillserver.storage import SpillStore
.B from darpa_spillserver.signals import parse_signal, decode_event_word
.B from darpa_spillserver.novatime import parse_range, convert
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B darpa_spillserver
package implements the DARPA Spill Information Server. Its modules are layered
so that each is useful on its own, without running a server.
.SH MODULES
.SS darpa_spillserver.signals
The accelerator signal registry and the hardware's decode rules, ported from
.I NssSpillInfo::getSpillTypeFromEvent
in the
.B NovaSpillServer
package.
.TP
.BI decode_event_word( evt )
Decode a raw 16-bit event word to a
.BR SpillType .
.TP
.BI parse_signal( text )
Resolve
.BR $74 ", " 74 ", " 0x74
or a registry name to a
.B Signal
record.
.TP
.BI signals_for_type( spill_type )
Every signal decoding to that type. More than one means a stored record
carrying only the type is ambiguous.
.SS darpa_spillserver.novatime
Parsing human time expressions and converting between timescales. The
arithmetic is delegated to
.BR nova_time_decoder (3);
nothing here reimplements a conversion.
.TP
.BI parse_instant( text ", " now ", " tz ", " end_of_day )
Parse one time expression to NOvA ticks.
.TP
.BI parse_range( start ", " end ", " now ", " tz )
Resolve a pair into a half-open
.RI ( start ", " end )
tick range.
.TP
.BI convert( nova )
Render one tick count as a
.B ConvertedTime
carrying NOvA, UNIX, UTC and GPS forms.
.SS darpa_spillserver.storage
The SQLite archive.
.B SpillStore
is synchronous and thread-safe through per-thread connections; async callers
should wrap calls in
.IR asyncio.to_thread .
Inserts are idempotent on
.RI ( nova_time ", " spill_type ", " signal_code ).
.SS darpa_spillserver.tdu_client
An async HTTP client for the TDU's embedded web server, speaking both the
legacy single-event routes and the bulk
.I /spill_history
route, and tolerating the malformed JSON that
.B DumpSpillHistory
emits.
.SS darpa_spillserver.poller
The background ingest loop.
.SS darpa_spillserver.formats
CSV and JSON rendering, as streaming generators.
.SS darpa_spillserver.config
Configuration merged from defaults, a YAML file, the environment, and the
command line.
.SS darpa_spillserver.api ", " darpa_spillserver.app
The FastAPI routes and the application factory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read an archive directly:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from darpa_spillserver.storage import SpillStore
from darpa_spillserver.novatime import parse_range, convert
from darpa_spillserver.signals import parse_signal

store = SpillStore("spills.db")
start, end = parse_range("2026-07-01", "today")
signal = parse_signal("$74")

page = store.query(start_nova=start, end_nova=end,
                   spill_types=[signal.spill_type])
for event in page.events:
    print(convert(event.nova_time).utc)
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build an application for testing, without contacting a TDU:
.PP
.RS
.EX
from darpa_spillserver.app import create_app
from darpa_spillserver.config import Config

config = Config()
config.storage.path = ":memory:"
app = create_app(config, start_ingest=False)
.EE
.RE
